# `artifacts.patch`

Patch an artifact's metadata (name / owner / expiry).

**Policy** — command `[C1_WORKSPACE]`. Capability `ship.artifacts.write`.

## Arguments

| name | type |
|------|------|
| `id` | `string` |
| `name` | `string` |
| `owner_actor` | `string` |
| `expires_at` | `string` |

## Returns

`ArtifactRecord` (JSON).

| field | type |
|-------|------|
| `id` | `string` |
| `name` | `string` |
| `mime` | `string` |
| `size` | `number` |
| `path` | `string` |
| `scope` | `string` |
| `space_id` | `string` |
| `run_id` | `string` |
| `content_hash` | `string` |
| `expires_at` | `string` |
| `owner_actor` | `string` |
| `collection_id` | `string` |
| `item_id` | `string` |
| `created_at` | `string` |

## Invoke

```
ship ops call artifacts.patch --json '{ "id": "", "name": "", "owner_actor": "", "expires_at": "" }'
```

Kind: command.

## Example response

```json
{
  "id": "artifact-checkout-audit",
  "name": "checkout-audit-v2.md",
  "mime": "text/markdown",
  "size": 4096,
  "path": ".artifacts/checkout-audit.md",
  "scope": "project",
  "project_id": "harbor",
  "run_id": "job-checkout-flow-a1b2c3d",
  "owner_actor": "actor-rust-lane-harbor",
  "created_at": "2026-05-24T18:30:00Z"
}
```
